  component queries `wine_regions` directly.
- The 17 region names are no longer duplicated in TypeScript. The hardcoded
  `/esplora` array was deleted; `Tutte` survives only as an Explore UI
  pseudo-value in `src/lib/esplora/filtri.ts`, never in service or props data.
- `/vendi` Region is a canonical Select, required, with no free-text fallback.
  It is disabled unless the registry read succeeded non-empty; loading, empty
  success and read error are three distinguishable states. One wizard visit
  performs at most one registry read (promise held in a ref, Strict-Mode safe),
  and the Cantina path performs none because wine identity stays read-only.
  Step `Identificazione` cannot be left without a canonical Region: the guard is
  in the hook, not only in the markup.
- The AI catalog suggestion can no longer write arbitrary Region text.
  `campiDaSuggerimento` accepts the registry names and applies a Region only on
  an exact match after trim and case folding, writing the registry spelling
  (`toscana` and ` TOSCANA ` -> `Toscana`). `Toscanaa` and `Tuscany` are not
  applied and the current Region is preserved, empty included. No fuzzy
  matching, typo correction, translation or alias was introduced. Other AI
  fields are unchanged.
- `/esplora` starts listings and registry reads together and isolates the
  registry: an unexpected rejection is caught, so a registry failure or an empty
  registry never hides listings and never disables ordinary text search — the
  Region control degrades to a readable unavailable state. Ordinary search now
  matches a local in-memory haystack of `produttore`, `nome`, `denominazione`,
  `annata` and `regione`; Region filter, type, price, sorting, pairing mode and
  AI pairing are unchanged and Region and text compose.
